 ## Operating characteristics
-* **Time Complexity:** The complexity is determined by the number of streamlines $N$ and the number of clusters. Since each streamline is reduced to a fixed-size feature vector (9 dimensions for Stage 1, 2 dimensions for Stage 2), the complexity is $O(N \cdot K \cdot I)$ where $K$ is the number of clusters and $I$ is the number of iterations, rather than $O(N \cdot L \cdot K \cdot I)$ where $L$ is the number of points per streamline. This makes it efficient for large datasets [S1].
