 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Chen, Yan, Yu, Max, and Ma in 2011 in the paper "An Illustrative Visualization Framework for 3D Vector Fields" [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of existing vector field visualization techniques, which often assume no particular structure or require topological connectivity. The method builds on the concept of using entropy metrics (Linear and Angular Entropy) originally proposed by Furuya and Itoh [S1]. It is used in the context of illustrative visualization, specifically rendering streamlines as "streamtapes" to enhance depth perception and depict vicinity flow [S1].
